---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getRelease, repository } from "../lib/release";
const r = await getRelease();
---

<Layout
  title="Download VeyDock for Windows x64 | Official Alpha"
  description="Download the current real VeyDock Windows x64 installer from GitHub. Check its version, checksum, unsigned publisher status and setup requirements."
>
  <section class="page wrap">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE REAL BUILD / WINDOWS X64</p>
      <h1>Dock it on Windows.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The current public release, straight from GitHub. No sign-up. No
        download gate.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="download-panel">
      <div>
        <h2>
          VeyDock{" "}
          <span class="mono">{r.prerelease ? "PRERELEASE" : "STABLE"}</span>
        </h2>
        <a class="button" data-download href={r.url}>
          Download Windows installer <span>↓</span>
        </a>
        <div class="download-links">
          <a class="text-link" href={r.release}>
            Release notes ↗
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href={r.checksums}>
            Checksums ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <dl class="download-data">
          <div>
            <dt>VERSION</dt>
            <dd>{r.version}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>PLATFORM</dt>
            <dd>Windows / x64</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>INSTALLER SIZE</dt>
            <dd>{(r.size / 1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>PUBLISHED</dt>
            <dd>
              {new Date(r.date).toLocaleDateString("en-GB", {
                day: "numeric",
                month: "long",
                year: "numeric",
              })}
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>ACTUAL FILENAME</dt>
            <dd>{r.name}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>PUBLISHER SIGNING</dt>
            <dd>Unsigned public alpha</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        {r.stale && (
          <p class="notice">
            GitHub metadata could not be refreshed. Showing the last known
            release. Confirm it on GitHub before downloading.
          </p>
        )}
      </div>
      <div class="download-note">
        <h3>Before you run it.</h3>
        <p>
          The current alpha uses its historical installer name. That is the real
          file, not a different product.
        </p>
        <p>
          Windows may show Unknown publisher or SmartScreen warnings. Verify the
          source and checksum. Updater signatures do not replace Windows code
          signing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Codex Desktop, the Codex CLI and WebView2 are required. ARM Windows
          uses x64 emulation; there is no native ARM package.
        </p>
        <p>
          Source-code ZIP files are not installers. You do not need Node.js or
          Rust to use the compiled app.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/getting-started">
          The setup manual ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What you should know about this alpha</h2>
      <p>
        Real per-profile usage refresh has been observed. Complete real-desktop
        account-switch acceptance and installer-driven updating are still
        pending. Interface screenshots on this website show a newer development
        preview with simulated data, not a guarantee of the downloadable build’s
        appearance.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/VERIFICATION.md`}>
          Read the verification record
        </a>{" "}
        before depending on the app for important work.
      </p>
      <h2>How do later updates arrive?</h2>
      <p>
        The alpha has an update check and an explicit install action. Nothing
        silently rotates accounts or installs a new build. Until
        installer-driven updating passes real acceptance, use the latest
        official release installer to update. Saved Hub data is stored
        separately; keep a private backup of sensitive state.
      </p>
      <p>
        VeyDock is built for Windows. If you are browsing on a phone, open this
        page on the Windows computer where you want to install it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
